{"ref": "Bava Metzia 59b:7", "heRef": "בבא מציעא נ״ט ב:ז׳", "sectionRef": "Bava Metzia 59b", "indexTitle": "Bava Metzia", "heIndexTitle": "בבא מציעא", "categories": ["Talmud", "Bavli", "Seder Nezikin"], "next": "Bava Metzia 60a", "sectionNames": ["Daf", "Line"], "versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Wikisource Talmud Bavli", "license": "CC-BY-SA", "versionSource": "http://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%AA%D7%9C%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%93_%D7%91%D7%91%D7%9C%D7%99", "text": "מה עשה ר\"ע לבש שחורים ונתעטף שחורים וישב לפניו ברחוק ארבע אמות אמר לו ר\"א עקיבא מה יום מיומים אמר לו רבי כמדומה לי שחבירים בדילים ממך אף הוא קרע בגדיו וחלץ מנעליו ונשמט וישב על גבי קרקע"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Sefaria Community Translation", "license": "CC0", "versionSource": "https://www.sefaria.org", "text": "What did R. Akiva do? He dressed in black and sat before him at a distance of four Amot. R. Eliezer said: “Akiva, what is today from all days?” He said, “My master, it appears to me your friends distanced themselves from you.” R. Eliezer too tore his clothes, removed his shoes and sat on the ground"}], "available_versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "license": "CC-BY-NC", "versionSource": "http://sefaria.org"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "William Davidson Edition - English", "license": "CC-BY-NC", "versionSource": "https://korenpub.com/collections/the-noe-edition-koren-talmud-bavli-1"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Wikisource Talmud Bavli", "license": "CC-BY-SA", "versionSource": "http://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%AA%D7%9C%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%93_%D7%91%D7%91%D7%9C%D7%99"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualL